+
+Second, we have real-world evidence. Countries with price negotiations and universal healthcare—Germany, Switzerland, Australia—still have robust pharmaceutical innovation. The US model hasn't actually produced proportionally more breakthrough drugs; it's just enriched a few corporations. Meanwhile, foundational research that actually advances medicine comes largely from government-funded institutions like the NIH and universities.
+
